I have a bug in the orbit logic: `root` applies a -90° rotation so the clouds/paths/markers are added in world Z-up coords and rotated into view. But the camera, controls.target, water plane, and dive lines mix conventions. Let me fix this cleanly: put the water plane, paths, markers, dive lines all inside `root` (world coords), and compute camera/target in **view space** via the rotation. The orbit math operates in view space (camera.position/controls.target), which is correct since those are not inside root.

